    checks: [quiz('Which fact creates the clearest documentary ownership gap?', ['The paid freelancer has no signed assignment', 'The code has a product name', 'A database has 2,400 records'], 0, 'Payment is evidence of the commercial relationship; it does not by itself establish every transferred right.'), quiz('What makes the pricing method protection more credible?', ['Mark it secret and leave access open', 'Limit access, record permissions and use confidentiality terms', 'Publish it to prove ownership'], 1, 'A secrecy strategy depends on actual operational controls.'), quiz('What is the best exclusivity safeguard?', ['An unlimited territory', 'No termination right', 'Measurable sales milestones and review rights'], 2, 'Performance conditions reduce the risk of a distributor blocking a market.')],
    debrief: ['Employee ownership requires the applicable law and facts; do not turn silence into a universal rule.', 'Prioritise the interface assignment, manual contributors, brand clearance and exposed pricing method.', 'Novelty, government-source reuse and database rights remain jurisdiction-specific verification questions.'],
    rubric: ['All ten assets classified with missing evidence identified', 'Five priorities have commercial and legal reasons', 'Licence scope and source-code continuity are controlled', 'Plan has named owners, dates and budget']
